  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The laws of indices, simplifying and rationalising surds, and the full toolkit for quadratics — factorising, completing the square and the formula.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Algebra core",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( a^{m}a^{n}=a^{m+n} \\), \\( a^{-n}=\\tfrac{1}{a^{n}} \\), \\( a^{1/n}=\\sqrt[n]{a} \\). Quadratic formula \\( x=\\dfrac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\); the discriminant \\( b^{2}-4ac \\) fixes the number of real roots.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Indices",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^{m}a^{n}=a^{m+n} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Surds",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{ab}=\\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Completing square",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (x+\\tfrac{b}{2})^{2}-\\tfrac{b^{2}}{4} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Discriminant",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( b^{2}-4ac \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Simplify \\( \\sqrt{12} \\).</p>\\[ \\sqrt{4\\cdot3}=2\\sqrt{3}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Complete the square for \\( x^{2}+4x \\).</p>\\[ (x+2)^{2}-4. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Solve \\(2x^2-5x-3=0\\) by completing the square.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(2(x^2-\\tfrac{5}{2}x)=3\\Rightarrow2(x-\\tfrac{5}{4})^2-2\\cdot\\tfrac{25}{16}=3\\Rightarrow(x-\\tfrac{5}{4})^2=\\tfrac{73}{16}\\). Hmm — actually factor: \\((2x+1)(x-3)=0\\Rightarrow x=-\\tfrac{1}{2}\\text{ or }x=3\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
